{"files": [{"id": 25569105, "name": "12915_2020_905_MOESM13_ESM.pdf", "size": 112985, "is_link_only": false, "download_url": "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/25569105", "supplied_md5": "dac118b6d7d407d056f7c124d8862267", "computed_md5": "dac118b6d7d407d056f7c124d8862267", "mimetype": "application/pdf"}], "folder_structure": {}, "authors": [{"id": 9676479, "full_name": "Luisa Henkel", "first_name": "Luisa", "last_name": "Henkel", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 9676482, "full_name": "Benedikt Rauscher", "first_name": "Benedikt", "last_name": "Rauscher", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 476884, "full_name": "Barbara Schmitt", "first_name": "Barbara", "last_name": "Schmitt", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 3446093, "full_name": "Jan Winter", "first_name": "Jan", "last_name": "Winter", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 9676485, "full_name": "Michael Boutros", "first_name": "Michael", "last_name": "Boutros", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": "0000-0002-9458-817X"}], "custom_fields": [{"name": "Research Data Support", "value": "", "settings": {"validations": {"min_length": 1, "max_length": 250}, "placeholder": "Complete where RDS data are part of RDS submission"}, "field_type": "text", "order": null, "is_mandatory": false}], "figshare_url": "https://springernature.figshare.com/articles/journal_contribution/Additional_file_13_of_Genome-scale_CRISPR_screening_at_high_sensitivity_with_an_empirically_designed_sgRNA_library/13278597", "download_disabled": false, "description": "Additional file 13: Figure S8. Prediction of sgRNA DNA cutting activity based on control phenotypes. (A) Log2 fold change phenotype distributions for sgRNAs targeting nonessential genes (red) as well as targeting (blue) and non-targeting control sgRNAs (green) across different screens conducted with the HD CRISPR library. The screen with the HD CRISPR library A in HAP1 single cell clone SCC12, which was used for subsequent analyses, is highlighted in red. (B) Fit of a Gaussian mixture model with 4 components for screens in SCC12. Components 1 (yellow) and 2 (blue) represent non-targeting and targeting sgRNAs, respectively. Components 3 and 4 capture the phenotypes of sgRNAs with moderate and severe viability phenotypes. (C) Comparison of true fold change distributions of targeting and non-targeting sgRNAs (solid line) to the distributions estimated by the mixture model components (dashed lines) for both HD CRISPR libraries A and B. (D) Number of sgRNAs associated with each phenotype group targeting essential genes according to MAGeCK analysis. For this representation components 3 and 4 are combined in the red group \u2018target phenotype\u2019. sgRNAs are stratified based on their design: \u2018empirical essential\u2019 sgRNAs target context-specific essential genes and were selected for the HD CRISPR library based on their previous on-target phenotypes. \u2018Empirical nonessential\u2019 sgRNAs are part of previously published libraries and target broadly nonessential genes. They were selected based on their lack of outlier phenotypes. De novo sgRNAs were designed using the software cld [34]. (E) Similar plot as D showing sgRNAs of the HD CRISPR library B associated with each phenotype group.", "funding": "de.NBi BMBF", "funding_list": [{"id": 19470483, "title": "de.NBi BMBF", "grant_code": "", "funder_name": null, "is_user_defined": 1}], "version": 1, "status": "public", "size": 112985, "created_date": "2020-11-24T04:55:27Z", "modified_date": "2026-03-08T09:19:31Z", "is_public": true, "is_confidential": false, "is_metadata_record": false, "confidential_reason": "", "metadata_reason": "", "license": {"value": 47, "name": "CC BY + CC0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}, "tags": ["CRISPR/Cas9", "Genetic screens", "sgRNA design", "Gene essentiality", "Functional genomics"], "keywords": ["CRISPR/Cas9", "Genetic s